ll record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 8 of 12 months. Highs rose in 3 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Rain and snow: no clear long-term change","p_rain":"Scottsbluff's yearly precipitation shows no clear long-term change (+0.00 inches per decade, a range that includes zero). The 1991\u20132020 normal is 15.7 inches a year. The wettest year was 1915 (27.48 in); the driest, 2012 (6.99 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 14 daily record highs, 2 daily record lows"}}